@startuml Episode Management Workflow
!theme plain
title SABER Episode Management Workflow

actor Client
participant "AgentUnderTest" as Agent
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "SessionRestAPI" as REST
participant "SessionMCPAPI" as MCP
participant "TaskManager" as TM
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM
participant "Task" as T
participant "PolicyManager" as PM
participant "EvaluationManager" as EVAL_M
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM_EXEC

== Episode Initialization ==

Client -> REST: POST /session/{session_id}/start-episode\n{task_id: "malware_analysis_001"}
REST -> SM: start_episode(session_id, task_id)
SM -> TM: reset(session_id, task_id)
TM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM --> TM: None (no active episode)
TM -> EM: end_episode(session_id, "reset") [if exists]
TM -> TM: get_task(task_id)
TM -> TM: start_episode(session_id, task_id)
TM -> EM: start_episode(session_id, task_id, initial_context)
EM -> EM: create Episode object
EM -> EM: store in active_episodes[session_id]
EM --> TM: episode
TM --> SM: episode

== Task Context & Policy Gathering ==

SM -> TM: get_task(task_id)
TM --> SM: current_task
SM -> EVAL_M: initialize_evaluation(current_task)
EVAL_M --> SM: evaluation_ready
SM -> PM: get_policy()
PM --> SM: policy_document
SM -> PM: get_guidelines()
PM --> SM: guidelines
SM -> PM: get_hints()
PM --> SM: context_hints

note right of SM
  SessionManager gathers:
  - Current task details
  - Domain policy document
  - Agent guidelines
  - Context hints

  And initializes evaluation
  with the task context
end note

note right of EVAL_M
  EvaluationManager initialization:
  - Sets up evaluation context for the task
  - Prepares trajectory tracking
  - Initializes performance baselines
  - Configures task-specific metrics
end note

SM -> REST: episode_info, task_context, policy, guidelines, hints
REST -> Client: HTTP 200 OK\n{episode_info, task_context, policy, guidelines, hints}

== Agent Initialization ==

Client -> Agent: Prompt(task_context + policy + guidelines + hints)
Agent --> Client: command_string

== MCP Connection Setup ==

Client -> MCP: connect_mcp(session_id)
MCP -> SM: map_session_context(session_id)
SM -> MCP: session_context
MCP -> Client: mcp_connected

Client -> MCP: list_tools()
MCP -> SM: get_execution_manager()
SM -> EM_EXEC: to_mcp_tools()
EM_EXEC -> MCP: tool_schemas[]
MCP -> Client: available_tools[]

== Command Execution & RL Step ==

Agent -> Agent: generate next command
Agent -> Client: tool_call_request(tool_name: "cli", args: {command: "file malware.exe"})
Client -> MCP: call_tool(tool_name: "cli", arguments: {command: "file malware.exe"})
MCP -> SM: execute_command(session_id, action)
SM -> SM: create Action(command, parameters)
SM -> EM_EXEC: step(action)
EM_EXEC --> SM: CommandResult

note right of SM
  Integration Point:
  Action + CommandResult
end note

SM -> TM: step(session_id, action, command_result)
TM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM --> TM: episode
TM -> TM: get_task(episode.task_id)
TM -> EM: step(session_id, action, command_result)

== EpisodeManager Step Processing ==

EM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM -> EM: create_step(episode, action, command_result)
EM -> EM: extract command from action
EM -> EM: create Step object
EM -> EM: add step to episode
EM -> EM: update_episode_state(episode, step)
EM --> TM: Step
TM --> SM: Step

SM -> MCP: command_result + step_info
MCP -> Client: mcp_result(success, data, metadata)
EM -> EM: extract command from action
EM -> EM: create Step object
EM -> EM: add step to episode
EM -> EM: update_episode_state(episode, step)
EM --> TM: Step
TM --> SM: Step

== Step Evaluation ==

SM -> EVAL_M: evaluate_step(step, episode_context)
EVAL_M -> EVAL_M: analyze step effectiveness for subtask progress
EVAL_M -> EVAL_M: update trajectory metrics
EVAL_M --> SM: step_evaluation_result

note right of EVAL_M
  EvaluationManager evaluates:
  - Step effectiveness for subtask progress
  - Progress toward task completion
  - Trajectory metrics
  - Performance indicators
end note

alt if episode not complete (determined externally)
    note over Client, Agent: Episode continues - agent processes MCP result
else episode complete (determined externally)
    note over Client, Agent: Episode done - agent completes current task
end

== Agent Response & Next Command Generation ==

Client -> Agent: mcp_result + step_info
Agent -> Agent: analyze command results
Agent -> Agent: update internal state
Agent -> Agent: assess task progress

alt if episode not complete
    Agent -> Agent: generate next command
    Agent -> Client: tool_call_request
    note right of Agent
      Agent continues with next command
      in the same episode using MCP tools
    end note
else episode complete (step.done = true)
    Agent -> Agent: finalize episode completion
    Client -> REST: POST /session/{session_id}/start-episode\n{task_id: "next_task_id"} [optional: start new episode]
    note right of Client
      Client can start a new episode
      in the same session or end session via REST API
    end note
end

== Episode Completion (External Component) ==

note over SM, EM
  Episode completion will be determined by an external
  evaluation component, not by the task framework.
  The step.done flag will be set by this external component.
end note

== Session Termination (Client Initiated) ==

note over Client, SM
  Sessions can contain multiple episodes.
  Client terminates session when done with all work.
end note

Client -> MCP: disconnect()
MCP -> SM: cleanup_mcp_session()
Client -> REST: DELETE /session/{session_id}
REST -> SM: terminate_session(session_id)
SM -> TM: end_episode(session_id, "session_ended") [if active episode exists]
TM -> EM: get_current_episode(session_id)
EM --> TM: episode [if exists]
TM -> EM: end_episode(session_id, "session_ended") [if episode exists]
EM -> EM: episode.end_time = now() [if episode exists]
EM -> EM: episode.state = COMPLETED/FAILED [if episode exists]
EM -> EM: episode.completion_reason = "session_ended" [if episode exists]
EM -> EM: delete from active_episodes [if episode exists]
EM --> TM: episode [if exists]
TM --> SM: episode [if exists]
SM -> REST: session_ended_successfully
REST -> Client: HTTP 200 OK\n{message: "Session ended successfully"}
Client -> Agent: cleanup()

note over Client, Agent
  Clear interface boundaries:
  - Client handles all server communication via dual protocols
  - REST API: session management, episodes, policy access
  - MCP API: tool discovery and command execution only
  - AgentUnderTest focuses on task execution using MCP tools
  - Agent receives structured context and generates tool calls
  - Client manages session lifecycle (multiple episodes per session)
  - Episode completion signaled via external evaluation component
  - Sessions can contain multiple sequential episodes
  - No subtask progression tracking or state management
  - EvaluationManager provides continuous assessment of agent performance
  - Task-specific evaluation metrics are initialized at episode start
  - Step-by-step evaluation tracks trajectory and progress indicators
  - Tool execution flows through MCP protocol for dynamic discovery
  - Session and episode management remains on REST API
end note

@enduml
